WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.530
Hi! A hibiscus has flowers, but does a fern? Today we'll learn how to sort plants into flowering and non-flowering plants.

2
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:17.106
Flowering plants make flowers. A flower can become a fruit, and the fruit holds seeds.

3
00:00:17.256 --> 00:00:21.930
Hibiscus, mango trees and rice are all flowering plants.

4
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.762
Some flowering plants have tiny flowers, like grass and rice, but they still flower.

5
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:32.874
When seeds are planted, they can grow into new plants.

6
00:00:33.024 --> 00:00:37.914
Ferns and mosses never flower. They reproduce by spores.

7
00:00:38.064 --> 00:00:43.218
Turn over a fern leaf and you'll see little dots. They hold the spores.

8
00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:48.042
Pine trees don't flower either. Their seeds grow in cones.

9
00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:53.250
When sorting plants, ask: does it make flowers?

10
00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:00.042
Watch out! Some pupils think plants without flowers can't reproduce. That's wrong!

11
00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:05.610
Ferns and mosses reproduce by spores, and pine trees have seeds in cones.

12
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.530
Even without flowers, they can make new plants.

13
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:18.930
Your turn! Is a mango tree a flowering plant? Pause and think.

14
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:27.378
Yes. A mango tree flowers and makes mangoes, which have seeds inside. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:27.528 --> 00:01:35.610
Another one! How do ferns reproduce? Pause and think.

16
00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:44.538
Ferns never make flowers. They reproduce by spores, which are tiny, like dust. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:52.674
Here's another! Do mosses have flowers? Pause and think.

18
00:01:52.824 --> 00:02:00.234
Mosses don't flower. They also reproduce by spores. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:08.778
Try one more! Where do a pine tree's seeds grow? Pause and think.

20
00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:16.554
A pine tree's seeds grow in cones. Pine trees don't flower. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:16.704 --> 00:02:28.386
Try one more! Turn over a fern leaf. There are little dots underneath. What is inside them? Pause and think.

22
00:02:28.536 --> 00:02:37.314
The dots hold spores. When spores land somewhere damp, they can grow into new ferns. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:37.464 --> 00:02:46.602
Last one! Is grass a flowering or non-flowering plant? Pause and think.

24
00:02:46.752 --> 00:02:54.954
Grass has tiny flowers, but it does flower. So it's a flowering plant. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:55.104 --> 00:03:04.626
Remember: flowering plants make flowers and fruits with seeds. Ferns and mosses reproduce by spores, and pines have seeds in cones.

26
00:03:04.776 --> 00:03:09.810
Go to a park and find a flowering plant and a fern!

